docs {
  # POST /webhooks/ourlens/ — Ingest an Ourlens order submission

  Ingests the n8n `mapping` payload into the CRM: creates/reconciles the
  Order, Organization, Rep, Contacts, Address, pilot OrderItem(s) and
  InvitationCode(s), and writes a `FormWebhookEvent` audit row. The endpoint
  itself returns an empty 200 body on success.

  ## Auth (deviation from the vendored DRF guide)

  This endpoint validates `body.token` inside the JSON body — NOT an
  `Authorization: Token` header. So this request uses `auth: none` and the
  token is supplied in the body as `"token": "{{token}}"`, read from the active
  environment. See `docs/django-bruno.local.md`.

  ## Status codes

  - `200 OK` — ingested (created or updated); empty response body. Also returned
    with status `rejected` when `mapping` is empty (n8n does not retry).
  - `400 Bad Request` — wrong content-type or unparsable JSON
  - `403 Forbidden` — missing or wrong `token`
  - `500 Internal Server Error` — ingestion failed (audit row status `error`)

  ## Request

  ```json
  {
    "token": "<secret>",
    "event": "create",
    "mapping": { "...55 descriptive keys..." },
    "executionMode": "production"
  }
  ```

  `executionMode` may be `production` or `test`; both are processed. `mapping`
  carries the order, rep, address, contacts, pilot product block and invitation
  codes (see `ourlives/docs/form-webhook.md`).
}